  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The test `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` in `tests/outcomes.rs` (lines ~199–229) cites `requirements.ci.fixme_stale_input` and covers the example's scenario.\n\n**Setup.** `fixture()` (lines ~9–62) writes `observed.txt` containing the comment `// FIXME(#125): timeout retries are untested; ...`.\n- The `requirements.timeout` example record has determination `{\"FIXME\": [\"#125\", \"rust-lang/rust#123\"]}`.\n- That record's only input is a file-range input (`observed.txt`, lines 1–1) whose text is that comment.\n- `valid_fixme_remains_visible_in_status_info_and_book` and `fixme_requirements_accept_issue_references_and_other_content` show that this unmodified record is accepted as a valid FIXME.\n\n**Action.** The test rewrites `observed.txt` to `changed source`. This changes the source comment inside the recorded range. The record's determination stays FIXME.\n\n**Assertions.**\n- `validate_repository` returns an error containing \"input text changed\". This matches the requirement that CI rejects the record because the recorded text no longer matches (`requirements.ci.inputs`), and that FIXME does not excuse stale evidence (`requirements.ci.determination`).\n- The status output marks the `requirements.timeout` row as `Invalid`. It still shows `#125` and reports \"input text changed\", so the changed input is surfaced.\n- Validation is run through `habeas::validate_repository` and `status_markdown`. Neither call runs a model, and the test does not reassess the gap. This matches \"without running a model or reassessing the documented gap\".\n\n**Minor gap.** This test does not assert that validation passes before the edit. The other FIXME tests cover that precondition.\n\n**Extra coverage.** The test also checks that FIXME does not excuse an uncovered reference: after adding a `{cite}` in `other.txt`, it expects a \"no input covers\" error. This is consistent with the cited `requirements.ci.determination`.\n\nThe scenario, the setup and the expected outcomes are all covered, and the test references the example directly.",
